<p>President Trump said the United States is talking with Iran but is not ready to accept terms to end the war, while Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi rejected the idea that Tehran had sought a ceasefire or had any reason to negotiate with Washington. The exchange came as the conflict entered its third week and both sides kept up their strikes. Several reports said the opening US-Israeli attacks on February 28 killed Iran’s supreme leader Ali Khamenei and other senior officials, sharply escalating the crisis. The war’s effects are spreading well beyond the battlefield. Reports say Iran is prepared to negotiate passage for selected oil tankers through the Strait of Hormuz, even as regional oil exports have been disrupted, fuel prices have risen worldwide and global air travel has been thrown into disarray. Gulf states have also faced spillover attacks, though one sign of resilience came when authorities contained a fire in Dubai linked to the wider conflict, limiting further damage there. US officials have projected that the war could end quickly, but Iranian officials say they are prepared for a long conflict. That gap underscores how far apart the two sides remain, and how difficult it may be to turn public messaging into diplomacy.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/34co2KNhBg9gzUv-aSdrIvjL5Vk1mXU5ZldLVcnrTYiyA3H-n_M7P_cWzi3OY_QWJvTxRPKvLltD4IMlxPQ28GnP5Gof8eUyMQOFVztTMx3zy2DqAPS6Nn-3DJK9iueCSeWSwBOlv6yygq4CwLrU9avIwt4RTG5-VnWb8cCR_we6yq05OIihwknn2ei1c2dWUwjV_5DuZegbtcKC4bdybYtiD2US2Ui1Nq3RkwaSqQZvT6zPTR16LKKsCQ' alt='President Donald Trump speaks to reporters aboard Air Force One en route from West Palm Beach, Florida, to Joint Base Andrews, Maryland, on March 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>NATO pressure: President Trump called for help from NATO allies as the fighting expanded, giving the crisis a broader transatlantic dimension.</li><li>Kharg risk: The Hindu reported that President Trump suggested the US might strike Kharg Island, signaling that core Iranian oil-export infrastructure could become a direct target as the war escalates.</li><li>IRGC threat: The Hindu reported that Iran’s Revolutionary Guards vowed to hunt down and kill Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, a sign that the conflict’s rhetoric is hardening alongside the military campaign.</li><li>Asia diplomacy: Firstpost reported that President Trump hinted at postponing a meeting with Chinese leader Xi Jinping as the Iran war took up more US attention.</li></ul><blockquote>We don&#x27;t see any reason why we should talk with Americans - Abbas Araghchi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: President Trump said the US is in discussions with Iran, but argued Tehran is not yet ready for a deal and that Washington wants better terms before ending the war. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-trump-says-us-talking-to-iran-but-tehran-not-ready-for-deal-to-end-war-11220812#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi: Araghchi said Tehran had not asked for a ceasefire and was prepared for a long war if necessary, casting endurance as leverage against Washington. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iranian-foreign-minister-abbas-araghchi-interview-trump-face-the-nation/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>US officials: US officials predicted the war could end quickly, a view that contrasts sharply with Tehran’s claim that it can outlast its opponents. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-officials-predict-quick-end-to-iran-war-while-tehran-says-it-can-outlast-foes'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-iran-war-live-updates-saudi-arab-qatar-dubai-missiles-drones-attack-iran-fm-says-strait-of-hormuz-open-to-all-but-enemies-claims-us-is-begging-for-help-liveblog-13989606.html'>US Iran War Live Updates: Trump hints at postponing meeting with Xi as Iran conflict escalates</a> - firstpo